@page "/"

<PageTitle>BlazorDnd</PageTitle>

<div class="example">
    <h1>BlazorDnd</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        A native Blazor drag-and-drop library inspired by
        <a href="https://react-dnd.github.io/react-dnd" target="_blank">React DnD</a>.
        It brings the same data-driven model &mdash; items, types, monitors and a pluggable
        HTML5 backend &mdash; to Blazor as idiomatic components.
    </p>

    <h2>Core concepts</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Items &amp; Types</strong> &mdash; you drag <em>data</em> (an item object) of a certain <em>type</em> (a string), not a view.</li>
        <li><strong>Monitor</strong> (<code>BlazorDndIDndMonitor</code>) &mdash; exposes live drag state: <code>IsDragging</code>, <code>IsOver</code>, <code>CanDrop</code>, offsets, the item, and more.</li>
        <li><strong>Components</strong> &mdash; <code>&lt;BlazorDndDndProvider&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;BlazorDndDraggable&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;BlazorDndDropTarget&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;BlazorDndDragLayer&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;BlazorDndDragHandle&gt;</code> map to React DnD's hooks.</li>
        <li><strong>Backend</strong> &mdash; built on Blazor's native HTML5 drag events.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Quick start</h2>
    <p>Register the service in <code>Program.cs</code>:</p>
    <pre><code>builder.Services.AddBlazorDnd();</code></pre>

    <p>Then wrap a region in a <code>BlazorDndDndProvider</code> and declare sources and targets:</p>
    <pre><code>@_quickStart</code></pre>

    <p>Pick an example from the sidebar to see it in action.</p>
</div>

@code {
    private const string _quickStart = @"<BlazorDndDndProvider>
    <BlazorDndDraggable TItem=""string"" Type=""BOX"" Item=""@(""crate"")"" Context=""d"">
        <div class=""box"" style=""opacity:@(d.IsDragging ? 0.4 : 1)"">Drag me</div>
    </BlazorDndDraggable>

    <BlazorDndDropTarget TItem=""string"" Accept=""BOX"" Context=""t"" OnDrop=""HandleDrop"">
        <div class=""dustbin"">@(t.IsOver ? ""Release!"" : ""Drop here"")</div>
    </BlazorDndDropTarget>
</BlazorDndDndProvider>";
}
